{"chunk_id": "d1d3fa6f4e61", "text": "Markandeya continues recounting the backstory behind the Ramayana events to Yudhishthira. Earlier divine arrangements are described: the asura Dundubhi is reborn as the scheming hunchback Manthara, while gods sire powerful monkey and bear heroes destined to aid Rama. The narrative then shifts to Ayodhya. King Dasaratha, proud of his virtuous and beloved eldest son Rama, decides to install him as prince-regent. Manthara overhears the plan and manipulates Queen Kaikeyi, convincing her that Rama\u2019s coronation will ruin her and her son Bharata. Reminding Dasaratha of a past promise, Kaikeyi demands two boons: Bharata\u2019s coronation and Rama\u2019s fourteen\u2011year exile to the forest. Bound by his word, the king is devastated, but Rama willingly departs with Sita and Lakshmana to preserve his father\u2019s honor. Dasaratha dies of grief, while Bharata condemns the deed and sets out to bring Rama back.\nManthara incites Kaikeyi to demand Rama\u2019s exile and Bharata\u2019s coronation; Rama accepts exile to uphold his father\u2019s promise, leading to Dasaratha\u2019s death and Bharata\u2019s grief.\nThemes: exile of Rama, manipulation and intrigue, dharma and filial duty, royal succession, grief and remorse", "vector": [0.0019204949494451284, -0.024257458746433258, -0.005969608668237925, -0.008412952534854412, -0.02391904406249523, 0.011018733493983746, -0.026937689632177353, -0.002230142941698432, -0.02529977075755596, -0.002541483147069812, 0.009989957325160503, 0.01026068814098835, 0.0019678727257996798, 0.03606130927801132, -0.00735033443197608, 0.005874853115528822, 0.05043710395693779, -0.01483603473752737, 0.02026418223977089, -0.008744597434997559, -0.008297891356050968, -0.004270774777978659, -0.007262347266077995, 0.00812868494540453, -0.015742981806397438, 0.008622768335044384, 0.028507927432656288, -0.02842670865356922, 0.017827607691287994, -0.010450199246406555, -0.015093228779733181, -0.004727632272988558, 0.